# Run 115 auto-queue daily cap — RED evidence

## Phase 1: missing seam (setup failure)
command: corepack pnpm exec vitest run test/run115-auto-queue-cap.test.ts
result: suite failed to import ../src/queue-runtime/auto-queue.js (module did not exist).
This is setup evidence only; it is not the behavioural RED.

## Phase 2: behavioural RED with the seam stubbed
A temporary stub exposed resolveAutoQueueDailyCap/applyAutoQueueDailyCap but returned the
default and did not apply a cap, and the config parser/renderer did not know the replay section.
command: corepack pnpm exec vitest run test/run115-auto-queue-cap.test.ts
result: 4 collected tests failed behaviourally:
  - defaults the readback to 100 and renders the section: expected undefined to equal
    { autoQueue: { dailyCap: 100, enabled: true } }
  - round-trips a configured cap: expected undefined to be 25
  - reads the cap from persisted config: expected 100 to be 7
  - applies the cap to the replay ledger ceiling: expected { dispatchesPerDay: 300 } to equal
    { counterfactualsPerDay: 7, dispatchesPerDay: 300 }

## Root gap
The replay loop already offers admitted captures to replay.dispatch and the ledger already has a
daily counterfactual ceiling (default 100), but the cap was env/constant-only and absent from the
runtime config readback, so the Learning Overview could not read or change it.
